  "id": "COMPOUND:34199 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Plicatilisin D appears to have a direct relationship with DNA polymerase iota, as it is the target of multiple entities that ultimately lead to this enzyme. The evidence suggests that Plicatilisin D acts as a target of 3-Hydroxypicolinic Acid and 17-[(E)-5,6-dimethylhept-3-en-2-yl]-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-tetradecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-ol, both of which are known to target DNA polymerase iota. This indicates a potential pathway where Plicatilisin D may inhibit DNA polymerase iota through the action of these intermediates. The consistent presence of DNA polymerase iota as a target across multiple pathways supports a functional link, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible dependency on these intermediates, suggesting that Plicatilisin D may exert its effect by modulating the activity of DNA polymerase iota through a complex network of molecular interactions.",
